




(LLM ↔ External APIs)

Flow:

User ----> LLM ------> Cloud/Connector------> External APIs -----> back to User.

Meaning:

This diagram shows a generic setup where an LLM is connected to multiple external APIs.

The LLM acts as the reasoning engine.

A connector or orchestration layer calls APIs (like Weather API, Database API, Cloud services).

The API responses flow back into the LLM, which formats the final user response.

Use Case: A chatbot that uses LLM + APIs (weather, finance, database lookups).
Focus: Generalized interaction (many APIs possible).

